      "content": "8.1 Road Network"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Punjab is served by two international airports: Sri Guru Ram Dass Jee International Airport (Amritsar) and Shaheed Bhagat Singh International Airport (Mohali).",
        "The state's railway network primarily falls under the Firozpur and Ambala divisions of the Northern Railway Zone.",
        "Ludhiana serves as the key inland container hub and the northern terminus of the Eastern Dedicated Freight Corridor (EDFC).",
        "Domestic civil enclaves under the UDAN scheme operate at Bathinda, Pathankot, Adampur (Jalandhar), and Sahnewal (Ludhiana).",
        "The Amritsar-Kolkata Industrial Corridor (AKIC) is a crucial infrastructure project driving industrial growth along the transport networks."
      ],
      "id": "45cih8y"
    },
